ck  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified    See note     Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  156  to  chromosome 17 signals  110  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than  2 0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for  chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis     The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of  Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID        Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH  23   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 13 36PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART A  Breast  Left   Excision  PART B  Breast  Right   Excision  PART C  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision  PART D  Axillary Skin  Right   PART E  Breast  Right  Deep Margin   Excision  PART F  Breast  Right  Medial Margin   Excision  PART G  Breast  Right  Lateral Margin   Excision  PART H  Breast  Right  In       report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1 INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM INKED SURFACES  AND FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN 6 OF 8 SLIDES   EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  3 RADIAL SCAR  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Calcifications are associated with the DCIS  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy with a 0 6cm white gray  ill defined area abutting the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A H  with the nodule in cassette B D  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
