opsy cavity  Labeled  Left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fibrofatty axillary node dissection containing approximately eighteen nodules  0 2cm in diameter to 1 0cm in diameter  All nodules are soft to focally firm  and tan pink  submitted in F through K  Labeled  Left additional axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of adipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ill defined thickening in the adipose tissue  entirely in L  SECTION CODE  A  closest margin of biopsy cavity  superior  B  skin and biopsy cavity  C E  representative sections of biopsy cavity  F K  axillary lymph nodes  L  tissue from additional axillary contents  M Q  additional sections of biopsy cavity  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION PART B  ADIPOSE TISSUE LEFT AXILLA  EXCISION    report_end  , Primary.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  14 MAY 97 at 18 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a left mastectomy specimen  attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin ellipse on the anterior aspect  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left axillary tail  The skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nipple and unremarkable epidermal surface  The breast parenchyma contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow  firm stellate mass in the medial inferior aspect of the specimen  extending to 0 6cm from the posterior  deep  resection margin  3 0cm to the inferior resection margin  3 0cm to the anterior  superficial  margin  4 0cm to the medial resection margin  8 0cm to the superior resection margin  and 4 0cm inferomedial to the nipple areolar complex  The remaining breast parenchyma contains multiple fibrous areas  predominantly in the lateral aspect of the breast  The axillary tail contains multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in dimension  SECTION CODE  A  mass with the closest  posterior deep  resection margin  B D  a cross section of the mass with cut surface inked blue  D F  a cross section of the mass with the cut surface inked blue  G H  inferior lateral fibrous area  I J  superolateral fibrous area  K O  axillary lymph nodes Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  G  Gregory Gallico III  M D  Daniel N Driscoll  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 24 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  FORMING TWO NODULES REMOVED_DATE CM AND REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The two nodules appear identical histologically and therefore probably represent independent foci of invasion originating from a single neoplastic population  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an indistinct firm area and a localizing wire in place   No accompanying radiograph   Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular tan firm lesion  extending to within 0 5cm of surface ink  There is adjacent parenchymal hemorrhage  Sections of mass in A through D  with other representative sections in E through J  Received labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue containing multiple tan rubbery lymph node as large as 1 1cm  submitted in cassettes K through N  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST EXCISION PART B  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
