s which abuts the posterior and medial margins and comes to 0 2cm of the inferior margin  0 3cm of the superior margin  1 5cm of the anterior margin  and is  2 0cm of the lateral margin  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  radial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved mammary tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  1 to closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between mass  1 and  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  2 to closest margins with the medial margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is a fragment of lobulated axillary fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm  On dissection  several tan pink lymph nodes are identified measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The larger lymph nodes are serially sectioned or bisected  All the lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2nd largest lymph node  serially sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3rd largest lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   All the smaller lymph nodes  submitted in toto  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday August 20   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 47 52PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday August 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 31 04PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCES