e sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows  D  Lateral most margin E  Full thickness F  Tumor to superior margin G  Tumor to posterior margin H I  Tumor to anterior margin J  Tumor to posterior margin K  Tumor to inferior margin L  Posterior inferior margin M  Medial most margin Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional deep margin left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal predominately dense white fibrous tissue with minimal yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as N S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 50  yellow lobulated adipose tissue to 50  dense white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as T X  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal predominately dense white fibrous tissue with minimal yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as Y DD  Gross Description by  BEN FARMER Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  GTM                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LEVEL REMOVED_DATE  529  PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN PART D  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  EXCISION PART E  BREAST LEFT INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  EXCISION , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 39 CLINICAL DATA  26 year old female status post right breast biopsy showing carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE   50     METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN FOUR OF TWENTY SEVEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  4 27   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The focus of infiltrating carcinoma  1 0cm in greatest dimension  is near the old biopsy site  however  it is a discreet nodule and may represent a second focus of infiltrating carcinoma  Surgical resection margins are free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 51                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen including the axillary tail  The overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 5 6cm  The nipple is 3 5cm from the medial margin of the ellipse and 2cm from both the superior and inferior margins of the ellipse  4 0cm lateral to the nipple is a diagonal healed incision line measuring 3 5cm  The remainder of the excised breast tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm thick  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  The superior margin is inked green  the inferior yellow and the deep black  Beneath the skin excision  there is a 1 5cm in diameter scarred region with intermixed chalky yellow fat necrosis representing the old biopsy site  At one edge of this biopsy site  there is a firm  hard yellow tan nodule measuring 1 0cm in diameter which is 0 5cm from the underlying deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of dense fibrous tissue with intermixed yellow to tan nodules  cysts scattered diffusely through it  These tan speckles measure approximately 0 1cm in diameter each  In the right upper outer quadrant there is a coalescence of these tan nodules speckles  This area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Multiple lymph nodes are found within the axillary tail region  These range in size from 0 1cm in greatest dimension to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  Grossly positive nodes are identified  SECTION CODE  A C  Biopsy cavity and close by 1cm hard nodules  D  Biopsy site  E  Adjacent area with coalescence of tan nodules  upper outer quadrant  F  Medial site tissue margin  G  Inferior skin margin  H  Superior skin and incision  IandJ  Nipple  K  Outer lower quadrant including deep margin  L  Inner lower quadrant  M  Inner upper quandrant  N S  Axillary lymph node  A representative section or all of each node is submitted in cassettes N through S  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  John D Mitchell  M D  G Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Primary.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right breast needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON THE GROSS SPECIMEN  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED SURFACE  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen SectionLab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy specimen containing a 1 5cm firm  tan  ill defined nodule approaching an inked margin  Representative with margin is frozen as FX 1  submitted in A  Tumor with margin in B  representative tumor in C and D  representative surrounding in E  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
