e characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm piece of breast with a needle localization wire placed  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with the short stitch superior  and the long stitch lateral  It is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  superior edge overinked orange  This specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a focal  firm  tan white mass located in the inferior mid portion of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and located 0 7cm from the posterior margin  0 6cm from the inferior margin and 1 0cm from the anterior margin  The mass is located  2 0cm from all other margins  The mass is surrounded by two areas of focal hemorrhage  consistent with biopsy site  The mass with surrounding hemorrhage is entirely submitted in A D  with closest margins  Further sections of focal hemorrhage consistent with biopsy site are submitted in E  Representative sections of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm area with multiple punctate calcifications located at the anterior margin are submitted in F and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shave inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue entirely submitted in H I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shave superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x2 5 x 1 5cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue entirely submitted in J K  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCI PART C  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCI , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on core biopsy  There are two tumors that have been identified  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3 OF 3  WITHIN AND BEYOND THE INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   ALL EXAMINED RESECTION MARGINS NEGATIVE FOR IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA  SURGICAL CLEARANCE   1 CM   HEALING BIOPSY SITES  2   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 34 OF 34 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEBORRHEIC KERATOSIS OF THE SKIN  NOTE  Two discontiguous tumors are present  with dissimilar morphology  consistent with two primary neoplasms  The invasive lobular carcinoma is negative for E cadherin by immunohistochemistry  The invasive ductal carcinoma is graded on the basis of both the current specimen and the prior biopsy  OS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the mitotic activity is more apparent in the biopsy  Hormone receptor and Her 2 studies will be performed on both tumors  blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is a 810 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse and nipple areola complex measuring REMOVED_DATE x 8 7cm  The axillary tail composes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm portion of the main specimen  There is a brown oval lesion on the white tan skin which is 2 0cm in diameter  raised 0 2cm from the surface of the skin  The anterior portion of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior black  Two irregular  somewhat ill defined nodules are identified within the breast  each is white pink  firm  and distinct from the surrounding yellow tan breast parenchyma  The first lesion  lesion  1  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and is located at the 12 o clock position approximately 6 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is 0 5cm from the deep margin  and greater than 2 0cm from the remaining margins  The second lesion  lesion  2  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located at the 10 o clock position approximately 3 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is greater than REMOVED_DATE from all of the margins  The two lesions are separated by 5 5cm  The tissue between the 2 mass lesions is mixed firm and fatty  with no apparent tumor involvement  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of lesion  1 and underlying closest relationship to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin  closest to lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue that is somewhat firm between lesion  2 and lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from medial portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from lateral portion of