Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 30 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   REGIONAL RESECTION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  METASTATIC TO 1 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 18                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Specimen is received in two containers each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Specimen  1  labeled  right breast mass  consists of a breast biopsy which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and weighs 44 grams  The specimen has not been oriented  Adherent to the breast biopsy is a skin ellipse which measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  In the skin ellipse there is a healed excisional surgical scar measuring 2 5cm in length and is centrally located within the skin ellipse  The specimen resection margins have been painted with India ink  The breast biopsy has been sectioned at 0 3cm intervals and reveals a firm  stellate mass consisting of   blem   white tissue  The tumor measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The tumor is located 0 4cm from the nearest deep surgical resection margin  The remainder of the breast biopsy shows unremarkable adipose tissue and breast tissue  The skin ellipse shows tan  wrinkled skin with a healed surgical incisional scar  there are no other focal abnormalities  The underlying tumor is located 0 2cm from the skin  Sections of this specimens will be submitted as follows  A F  sections through the breast tumor  submitted in total from one edge of the biopsy to the other   