 specimen is submitted in its entirety from superior to inferior in cassettes A F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast medial  final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety in cassettes G H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lateral  final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of tan yellow fibrofatty breast tissue which is submitted in toto in cassette I  Gross Description by  RYAN W  SCHNIEDERJAN Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXCI PART C  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXC , Primary.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    BOTH COMPONENTS APPROACHING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM  OF AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Roughly equivalent proportions of tubular  solid and cribriforming patterns are present in the infiltrative tumor  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present at a distance of more than one low power field from the main tumor  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The gross diagnostic impression is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  BIOPSY  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH SCANT BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab labeled  Right breast mass  is a breast biopsy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm  and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan firm area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  which is 1 1cm from the inked margin  No frozen section is performed and the specimen is submitted entirely in A through T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and designated  Right breast medial superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fatty tissue which is submitted entirely in U and V  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   SUSPICIOUS LESION  O R  Resident  Asif Rashid  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MEDIAL SUPERIOR MARGIN PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
