Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 30 CLINICAL DATA  Patient with history of lymphoma on FNA of breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  The lymphoma is composed of medium sized cells with round to irregular nuclei and a moderate amount of cytoplasm  The cells are smaller than those of typical large cell lymphoma and in areas resemble those of Burkitt like lymphoma  However the mitotic rate  while high  is less than typical Burkitt like lymphoma and  starry sky  histiocytes are not prominent  In addition  the Ki67 proliferation marker is positive in 50 70  of tumor cells  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  04 MAY 98 at 13 56                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibody to B lineage  antigen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of cells scattered within the tissue  The cells are also positive for Ki 67 in approximately 50 70  of the cells  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of B cell lymphoma  Added by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 98 at 18 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast nodule   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of tan pink to brown soft tissue  one half submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   now in cassette A  The remainder is submitted in cassette B  Gross Description by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Mark J Ott  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Diagnosis_(only_if_excisional_biopsy).
