Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 04 at 11 20 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision of invasive lobular carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  13 MAY 04 at 21 53                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan ellipse of skin which displays a 3 0cm linear well healed surgical incision  The short suture denotes the superior margin and a long suture the lateral margin  The superior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the medial margin with green ink  and the lateral margin with yellow ink  On sectioning  there is a 3 0cm in diameter biopsy cavity surrounded by firm  white fibrous tissue  The cavity is located in the mid portion of the specimen and the cavity is exposed along the superior aspect  The cavity is located 1 2cm from the lateral margin  1 8cm from the medial margin  0 6cm from the superior margin  and 0 6cm from the inferior margin  The cavity extends to 0 8cm of the anterior margin  and to 0 6cm of the posterior margin  The remainder of the tissue consists predominantly of firm  white fibrous tissue without focal lesion  The fibrous tissue comprises approximately 85  of the remaining tissue  Representative sections are submitted as  A D  Biopsy cavity  E F  Sections away from biopsy cavity  posterior aspect of specimen  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  DAVID COON  PhD