Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING MULTIFOCALLY TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is 1cm in greatest dimension  No unequivocal lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Estrogen receptor studies will be performed on formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tissue and will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   with attached specimen x ray   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing no gross lesion large enough to freeze  A 0 7cm ill  defined  slightly firm and gritty area is present at an inked margin  The nodule is submitted entirely in A through C  the remainder of the tissue in D through N  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
