e T  McKee MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm modified mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ellipse of skin with a centrally located unremarkable nipple  A long stitch marks the lateral aspect and a short stitch marks the superior aspect as designated by surgeon  The specimen is inked black  It is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm well defined  fleshy small mass with cystic areas underneath the brown tan skin ellipse  The mass is is 0 6cm from the deep margin  The entire mass is submitted in A D as follows  A  Mass in relation to closest deep margin  B  Mass in relation to deep margin  C  Mass in relation to anterior margin  D  Remaining representative sections of mass  Other sections are submitted as follows  E  Representative section away from mass  lateral aspect  F  Representative section away from mass  medial aspect  G  1 axillary lymph node  bisected  H  1 axillary lymph node  trisected  I  1 fatty lymph node  trisected  J  three lymph nodes  M  one lymph node N  possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  highest apical node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm adipose tissue  2 lymph nodes are identified and submitted as follows  K  1 lymph node  bisected  L  1 lymph node  Resident  SARAH ROLLINS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  WHITE 07 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  DANIELLE WALSH  MD PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE   HIGHEST APICAL    EXCISION , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
