cinoma component  supports that a minor component of invasive lobular carcinoma is present  It is this lobular component that extends to   0 1cm from the posterior margin  Immunoperoxidase stains for p63 and smooth muscle myosin heavy chain show staining of myoepithelial cells around the in situ carcinoma  Immunoperoxidase stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and ULEX Europaeus help confirm the presence of lymphatic invasion  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm left simple mastectomy specimen  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm tan white unremarkable portion of skin with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect  The nipple areolar complex measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with an unremarkable nipple  No scar is grossly appreciated  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a lobulated  tan pink focally hemorrhagic indurated to rubbery mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  The mass is located within the mid to medial aspect of the specimen and comes to 1 0cm from the free moving overlying black inked posterior margin and 3 0cm from the unremarkable skin surface  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to pink  lobulated and unremarkable with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  Along the periphery no lymph nodes are palpated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass with the closest posterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PRO