ified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 41 x 25 x 5 5cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 9 x 9 x 3cm axillary tail attached  consisting of fibroadipose tissue  A 40 x 20 5cm skin ellipse is present containing a 1 5cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  A stitch indicates superior  as designated by the surgeon  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  ill defined  firm white tan mass in the central posterior portion of the breast  An irregular area of central hemorrhage within the mass  1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    is present  The cut surface feels gritty  The mass extends to within 1cm of the posterior deep  closest  margin  The remainder of the breast reveals mostly lobular adipose tissue with thin  up to 0 5cm   fibrous strands interspersed  No further suspicious lesions are identified  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  Section Code  A C  Mass with closest posterior deep margin  D  Representative portion of mass   E  Closest margins to section D  overlying lesion  F G  Representative portions of grossly uninvolved breast tissue  H T  Lymph nodes  H P  Representative portion of one lymph node each  with fatty replacement  L N Q S  One bisected lymph node each  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  highest right axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node  The lymph node is bisected  the entire specimen is submitted in cassette U  Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   