esion which grossly abuts the posterior resection margin and is subjacent to and comes to within 1 5cm from the overlying scar  The cut surface medial to the lesion is approximately 80  of dense white fibrous tissue with a few 0 3cm scattered blue domed cysts  Lateral to the lesion is predominately 95  tan yellow adipose tissue with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm lymph node bearing axillary tail  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  stellate lesion to posterior margin C D  Representative section of lesion E F  Fibrous tissue medial to the lesion G  Fibrous tissue lateral to the lesion H  Six whole lymph nodes I  Three whole lymph nodes J  Two whole lymph nodes K L  One bisected lymph node each Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of tan yellow focally hemorrhagic adipose tissue fragments  There are no lymph nodes grossly identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes M N  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  EXCISION , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
