Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 15 CLINICAL DATA  Lobular carcinoma by outside hospital and reviewed at Brigham and Women s Hospital  suture at superior aspect                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus expands less than 0 2cm and does not transgress the lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Right breast  is a 20 x 15 x 3cm mastectomy specimen  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and areola complex  and a suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ill defined  tan white  firm area located in the medial aspect of the specimen  and focally extends to 0 3cm from both the anterior and posterior resection margin  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in cassettes A F  A C  Tumor in relationship to the closest anterior resection margin  D F  Tumor in relationship to the closest posterior resection margin   The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic changes  Representative sections of the fibrocystic area are submitted in cassettes G I  Labeled  Right axillary content  is a 7 x 5 x 1 5cm fatty adipose tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes J Q  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , Primary.
