Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast tumor                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The tumor has an unusual histologic appearance with a well circumscribed  expansile border  broad ribbons of tumor cells with focal spindled areas  and large geographic areas of necrosis  The tumor stains positively for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  keratin 7  CEA  and synaptophysin  and is negative for keratin 20  GCDFP 15  and chromogranin  These findings are consistent with a breast primary  however  they do not entirely exclude a metastatic lesion from another site  which should be considered in light of the unusual histology and lack of an in situ component  Clinical correlation is suggested  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  Grade  3  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the deep margin along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS SUPERIOR     EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR SHAVED MARGINS     EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 49                                                              