Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  LESION   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  90   WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  SLIDE B  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE  10     SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The carcinoma measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension and extends to inked resection margins  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present focally within and more prominently from the infiltrating carcinoma and focally extends to inked margins  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 42 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 26     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 99 at 14 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s  unit number  and  left breast lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm red yellow tan  fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen with a localizing wire in place  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white  firm area adjacent to the thick portion of metal wire  Representative section of firm area is frozen as FX 1 and  2  The remaining firm area is submitted in A through C  representative section of remaining tissue submitted in D through J  Frozen section  1 resubmitted in K  Frozen section  2 saved frozen  Resident  AJIT J  ALLES  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOM