Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a right breast mass  History of small cell carcinoma in the left breast diagnosed in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   100   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The focus of infiltrating carcinoma measures approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension  No blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire in place and accompanied by a roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  The specimen is submitted in A through K  No frozen section is done  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Diagnosis_(only_if_excisional_biopsy).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  LOCATED REMOVED_DATE CM OR GREATER FROM MARGINS  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    right mastectomy  short superior  long lateral    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  simple mastectomy specimen  with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm  tan white skin with a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm everted nipple  which is 0 5cm from the skin margin  There is a defect located between approximately 6 and 8 o clock  with an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm smooth  glistening  tan pink area  possibly consistent with an exposed cavity  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an open biopsy cavity at approximately 7 o clock  with surrounding gray white  rubbery tissue that extends to both the anterior and posterior margins  Additionally  at approximately 12 o clock and 11 0cm superior to the exposed biopsy cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic focus that is 1 0cm from the posterior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of yellow white  rubbery and focally nodular fibroadipose tissue  No other discrete lesions are identified  A few possible lymph nodes averaging 0 4cm in maximum dimension are palpated in the lateral aspect of the specimen  Additionally received are multiple fragments of tan white  unremarkable skin  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of hemorrhagic focus   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue intervening between the biopsy cavity and hemorrhagic focus   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of skin fragments   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 54 04PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , primary.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  MULTIFOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INVADING LYMPHATICS AND BLOOD VESSELS  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The largest tumor diameter is 3 7cm  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 28                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION OR BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   UNINTERPRETABLE SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    The assay was repeated 3 times  background was consistently high suggesting that there was a delay in tissue transport  that air drying occured  or that the tissue was not sent on wet ice  If S phase information is desired  flow cytometry should be attempted  Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  10 MAY 93 at 11 09     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 46 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 117 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 36     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm irregularly shaped piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hard  firm  yellow tan mass that extends to the margin  A touch prep is made  Tissue is taken for BRDU  estrogen receptors  A block is saved frozen  Representative sections of the mass are submitted in A through G  Additional sections of breast tissue are submitted in H through J  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  CARCINOMA O R  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
