Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 32 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  98   SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN TISSUE SECTION AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  2   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 7 x 4 x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with guide wire and accompanying x ray showing focal calcifications  In this region is a firm white tan nodule visible at the surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  non compressible white tan nodule with irregular border that appears hemisected at the surface  A representative fragment of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes A through Z  with nodule in cassettes A through D  A representative section of the firm peripheral nodule is also saved frozen  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Diagnosis_(only_if_excisional_biopsy).
