Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 MAY 94 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA   1 5 CM    SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Tumor comes within 0 2cm of the superior inked resection margin  Frozen section gross impression is confirmed  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  MICROCYTS AND ADENOSIS  AXILLA  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY OF TWENTY LYMPH NODES  2  BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 94 at 15 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast biopsy  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse attached  The short stitch designates superior  and a long stitch designates lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm  tan white  gritty  stellate lesion 0 2cm from the superior inked resection margin  The mass is 2 0cm from the deep resection margin  0 6cm from the lateral resection margin  3 0cm from the medial resection margin  and 1 8cm from the inferior resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The skin ellipse is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A C  representative sections of tumor in relation to superior inked resection margin DandE  representative sections of fibrosis with ink on superolateral resection margin F  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on lateral resection margin G  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on medial resection H  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on medial and inferior margins I  representative sections of skin ellipse  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axilla   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of fibrofatty tissue with fragments of skeletal muscle attached  Numerous soft  freely moveable lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm in greatest dime