 by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 890 grams  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  and an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan unremarkable skin ellipse  Located medially on the superior aspect of the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a suture designating 12 o clock  The specimen is inked  anterior blue  posterior black   serially sectioned displaying a fairly well circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm mottled tan to tan pink to focally yellow  focally necrotic mass located in the lower outer quadrant  abutting the posterior inked margin  9 5cm from the superior  5 0cm from the inferior  13 5cm from the medial  7 5cm from the axillary tail  and 2 0cm from the anterior  The remaining cut surfaces focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty lobulated breast tissue  There are no other masses grossly identified or palpated  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections and the entire lymph nodes are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   A C  Mass to posterior black inked margin  D  Mass towards anterior margin  E  Representative sections of fibrous tissue lateral to the mass  F  Representative section of fibrous tissue medial to the mass  G J  Whole lymph nodes  K Q  One bisected lymph node each  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RADICAL MODIFIED MASTECTOMY , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    4 CM BY GROSS EXAMINATION  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH APOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    COMEDO AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  WITHIN AND AWAY FROM THE INFILTRATING TUMOR  AND PRESENT AT A MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating component is not identified at a margin  Perineural invasion is identified  No lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is identified  Tumor infiltrating lymphocytes are moderate  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  METASTATIC TO THREE OF TWELVE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION FROM THE LARGEST NODE  2 CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x 5 x 3 5cm fragment of breast tissue with a 5 x 1 5cm puckered skin ellipse on one side  The specimen is inked and sectioned to show a 4 x 2 x 1 5cm centrally yellow  gritty ill defined mass which extends to within 0 5cm of the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved as frozen   Representative sections of tumor in A through E  additional representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma in F through J  Frozen section in K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla lymph node  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple palpable firm nodules  with two sutures attached at opposite ends  Sectioning into the tissue shows the presence of three large lymph nodes  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and several additional smaller lymph nodes  Representative sections of lymph nodes submitted in L through S  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                          